within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01X_OtherAntineoplasticAgents.L01XX44_Aflibercept;
model Aflibercept "Aflibercept — default model: Aflibercept_Thai2013_reference"
  extends Aflibercept_Thai2013_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of aflibercept: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01X_OtherAntineoplasticAgents.L01XX44_Aflibercept.Aflibercept_Thai2013_reference\">Aflibercept_Thai2013_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of aflibercept in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Aflibercept_Thai2013_reference</code></li></ul><h4>About aflibercept</h4><p>Aflibercept is used to treat several eye conditions involving abnormal blood vessel growth or swelling in the retina, such as wet macular degeneration, diabetic retinopathy, macular edema and retinal vein occlusion, and is also used for colorectal cancer. It is an approved medicine, authorised in the European Union for multiple eye and cancer indications, and is widely used in ophthalmology.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4689286\">Wikidata Q4689286</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Aflibercept\">Aflibercept</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 1382400, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Aflibercept;
